{
  "title": "Modified route account to load its page lazily",
  "context": [
    "The code of the account page was loaded when the app started, for every shopper, whichever page they opened. The app now loads that code the first time a shopper opens the account page. A shopper who only looks at the catalogue and the cart never loads it. The account page shows the same content as before.",
    "",
    "## Overview",
    "",
    "- **When** a shopper opens the catalogue or the cart, **then** [the app starts and does not load the module of the account page](code:src/router.tsx#L13). The app loaded that module at the start before.",
    "- **When** a shopper opens `/account` for the first time, **then** [the app loads the module of the account page and then renders the page](code:src/router.tsx#L13). The page was rendered with no load of its own before.",
    "- **When** the load of that module fails, **then** the account page does not render, and [the `account` route names nothing to render in its place](code:src/router.tsx#L13). The route has no `errorElement`.",
    "- **When** the account page is rendered, **then** nothing changes: it shows \"Loading your account…\" and then the profile form.",
    "- **When** the catalogue page or the cart page is rendered, **then** nothing changes: their routes still hold `element` and their static imports.",
    "",
    "## Implementation",
    "",
    "**`src/router.tsx`**",
    "",
    "- Removed the import of `AccountPage` from `@/routes/account`. `src/router.tsx` has no static import of the account page now.",
    "- Modified [the `account` route of `router`](code:src/router.tsx#router) to [hold a `lazy` function where it held `element: <AccountPage />`](code:src/router.tsx#L13). The function awaits `import(\"@/routes/account\")` and returns `AccountPage` as the `Component` of the route."
  ],
  "diff": [
    "diff --git a/src/router.tsx b/src/router.tsx",
    "--- a/src/router.tsx",
    "+++ b/src/router.tsx",
    "@@ -2 +1,0 @@ import { createBrowserRouter } from \"react-router\"",
    "-import { AccountPage } from \"@/routes/account\"",
    "@@ -14 +13 @@ export const router = createBrowserRouter([",
    "-      { path: \"account\", element: <AccountPage /> },",
    "+      { path: \"account\", lazy: async () => ({ Component: (await import(\"@/routes/account\")).AccountPage }) },"
  ],
